for genotyped material converted separately: \code{\link[=as_numeric]{as_numeric()}}'s default
\code{method = "frequency"} codes each dataset's own major allele as +1, so
separately converted founders and candidates can be reverse-coded at some
markers. Convert them together in one \code{\link[=as_numeric]{as_numeric()}} call, or separately with
\code{method = "reference"} and the same \code{ref_allele}. The coding is \strong{not
checked} -- it cannot be inferred from the dosages, since every candidate
genotype is possible at an informative marker -- and a reverse-coded marker
swaps the recurrent- and donor-homozygote calls there.
